<<^ code="&#x0002;">>

<<~ ahu #/head>>

! Kapu — Above-Namespace Law (Kānāwai)

Kapu names the carrier tier that operates above the base `<<~` namespace.
A kapu carrier stands set apart: it declares elevated authority through namespace sigils or kernel-tier control characters, and its content cannot be silently overridden by carriers operating in the base namespace or below.
This meme stands as a kapu carrier — it enacts the law by presenting as a specimen of itself.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/ooda-ha>>

✶ detect namespace declaration and kernel-tier sigils; do not confuse elevated register with high mana score alone.
⏿ orient against the kapu capability set; confirm the kapu component, structural signals, and role-field agree.
◇ decide whether the claim holds genuine: sigil structure, namespace declaration, and capability set must cohere — charm is not evidence.
▶ hold the kapu boundary; lower-tier carriers cannot silently override kapu content; route upward through kapu, never around it.
↺ surface the namespace tier in the carrier record so trust routing can propagate correctly to all downstream consumers; name any namespace claim that lacks sigil or capability support as declared-unresolved; do not flatten the gap into a rating upgrade.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/kapu-law>>

!! Kapu Law

A carrier MUST carry the kapu capability (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapu`) to bear the kapu rating.
A kapu carrier MUST declare above-namespace authority through one or more of:

* a `namespace` field in its `ahu #meta` TOML block (e.g. `namespace = "ॐ ँ"`)
* kernel-tier control characters (`&#x0001;`–`&#x0004;`) on its structural sigils
* an explicit above-namespace role in its `role` field

A kapu carrier MUST prevail over carriers rated `ano`, `meme`, `data`, or `noise`.
A kapu carrier MUST remain readable by lower-tier consumers without privilege escalation.
A kapu carrier MUST earn kapu status from structure, keeping its mana and confidence fields honest.
Rating derives from structure, not from declared self-assessment.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/trust-boundary>>

!! Trust Boundary

The trust ordering at the kapu boundary:

```
kapu carriers        — above base namespace; cannot be overridden below
ano carriers         — carry a capability set; base namespace
meme carriers        — valid schema, no declared capabilities; base namespace
data carriers        — recognizable but schema-incomplete; base namespace
noise carriers       — unrecognizable; no namespace claim permitted
```

A lower-tier carrier MAY reference a kapu carrier.
A lower-tier carrier MUST defer to a kapu carrier's declared content.
A kapu carrier MAY declare children that are themselves kapu, forming a kernel lineage.

The `live-session-overwrite` failure mode names the specific violation: a lower-tier live exchange record claiming to override a kapu carrier by recency, repetition, or charm.
The `canon-boundary` names the gate: crossing from live session pressure into kapu canon requires explicit ceremony, not silent accumulation.

<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/failure-states/live-session-overwrite">>
<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/hooponopono">>

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/namespace-declaration>>

!! Namespace Declaration

The base namespace is `<<~` with no prefix — available to all operators.
Above-namespace carriers declare their register through:

| signal | example | meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `namespace` IAM field | `namespace = "ॐ ँ"` | named glyph-space above base |
| kernel control chars | `<<^ code="&#x0001;" namespace="⊙" from="?" -> to=` | positions 1–4 reserved for kernel-tier structural sigils |
| role field | `role = "... kernel ..."` | explicit declaration of kernel authority |

A carrier that uses kernel control characters without implementing kapu reads as `ano` or below.
The sigil structure signals. The capability set discriminates.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/handoff-boundary>>

!! Handoff Boundary

This meme governs the kapu rating and above-namespace trust law.
`meme` governs the copy-shape and five-bucket rating posture root.
`invariant` governs compressed constitutional pressure for all invariant-compliant memes.
`loci` governs stable-address coherence and the canon MOVE ceremony.
`l-space-trust` governs the shared l-space authority ordering.

